  "value": "no native or token value moves here; what the call produces is three DEPLOYMENTS whose constructors run inside it - `CauldronCollection` (CauldronFactory.sol:71), `CauldronVault` (CauldronFactory.sol:75) and `RoyaltyRouter` (CauldronFactory.sol:81) - each created with caller-supplied addresses and none of them funded by this call.",
  "reachability": "UNGATED: any address can call it and get a collection plus a vault, because the factory grants no authority over an existing brew - the collection it creates takes its controller from the caller-supplied `c` (CauldronFactory.sol:72) rather than from msg.sender, and only the registry that calls it wires the result into the machine. In the protocol path the caller is the registry at `deployBrew` (CauldronRegistry.sol:1151). Three contracts are deployed here and each deployment is what confers the right the following lines spend: `CauldronCollection` (CauldronFactory.sol:71) makes this factory the collection's deployer, which is the only identity its configurator accepts at `setVault` (CauldronFactory.sol:76), `setRoyalty` (CauldronFactory.sol:82) and `setLiquidatorRenderer` (CauldronFactory.sol:87); `CauldronVault` (CauldronFactory.sol:75) is constructed with a zero floor offset and bound to the caller-supplied registry, so that registry - not this factory - is the address able to close it; and `RoyaltyRouter` (CauldronFactory.sol:81) is bound to the caller-supplied hook and is then installed as the collection's royalty receiver at `setRoyalty` (CauldronFactory.sol:82). The badge renderer is applied only when the factory's own slot is non-zero at `liquidatorRenderer` (CauldronFactory.sol:86), and this call is the only moment the factory holds that right. DERIVED: the three constructors execute with this factory as msg.sender, which is what the deployer checks behind those setters compare against."
 },
